<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theophilus I of Alexandria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 412</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theophilus was Patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> from 385 to 412. With imperial backing he led the campaign against paganism in the city, and in 391 the Serapeum, its greatest temple, was destroyed. He also helped depose John Chrysostom, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, at the Synod of the Oak in 403, and was succeeded by his nephew Cyril.</p></div>
